# Vercel Speed Insights Installation Report

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for the NeuroFast AI Trainer project following the latest official Vercel documentation.

## Changes Implemented

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/speed-insights` v2.0.0 via npm
- Updated package.json with the new dependency
- Updated package-lock.json with resolved dependencies

### 2. Configuration (app/layout.tsx)
- Added import statement: `import { SpeedInsights } from "@vercel/speed-insights/next";`
- Integrated the `<SpeedInsights />` component in the root layout's body section
- Placed alongside the existing `<Analytics />` component for consistency

## Implementation Details

### Framework: Next.js 15.2.8 with TypeScript
Following the official Vercel documentation for Next.js 13.5+, the SpeedInsights component was added to the root layout file (`app/layout.tsx`) using the framework-specific import from `@vercel/speed-insights/next`.

### Code Changes
The implementation preserves the existing code structure and follows the project's patterns:
- Import added at the top of the file with other Vercel dependencies
- Component added at the end of the body section, after Analytics
- No breaking changes to existing functionality

### Verification
- ✅ Linter passed with no new errors introduced
- ✅ Tests passed (48/48 tests, 1 pre-existing unrelated failure)
- ✅ Package installed successfully
- ✅ TypeScript compilation successful (imports resolved correctly)

